<title>USA: Sylvan to take $1.3 mln gain from lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Sylvan to take $1.3 mln gain from lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>SARVER, Pa. 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sylvan Inc said Wednesday it expects to record a one-time gain of about $1.3 million, or $0.20 per share, in the fourth quarter in connection with the settlement of a lawsuit.</p>
<p>The lawsuit was related to post-retirement medical benefits for hourly employees of Sylvan's defunct Moonlight Mushrooms Inc subsidiary.</p>
<p>The settlement between Sylvan and the United Steelworkers of America, AFL-CIO-CLC, was approved by the U.S. District Court for the western district of Pennsylvania on October 31, the company said.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Sylvan will pay the union $1,226,000 in a lump sum. In exchange, the union will release certain employment and benefit-related claims of the Moonlight retirees.</p>
<p>The non-cash gain is the result of the recalculation of the actuarial liability for post-retirement medical benefits.</p>
<p>Sylvan produces and distributes mushroom spawn.</p>
</text>
